  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nSome showers and thunderstorm may be ongoing across the far\nwestern portions of the area Wednesday morning but should push\noff to the south by the afternoon hours. The area will remain in\nthe upper level northwest flow pattern and another area of\nshowers and storms is expected to develop and push to the\nsoutheast Wednesday night into Thursday morning. The upper level\nridge will continue to push slightly back to the west during\nthis time so it is possible the activity Wednesday night remain\njust to the west of the area, but could again clip the far\nwestern portions of the area Wednesday night into Thursday\nmorning. Locally heavy rainfall will be possible. Scattered\nshowers and storms will remain possible west of Highway 65\nThursday afternoon and evening as times. \n\nAn upper level shortwave trough will move southwest across the \ncentral Plains Thursday night an across the region on Friday. \nAdditional showers and thunderstorms are expected to develop to \nthe west/northwest and move across the region. Coverage will \nlikely be better with this system as better forcing will be in \nplace. Locally heavy rainfall and localized flooding will be \npossible Thursday night into Friday as a band of showers and \nstorms will likely develop, the exact location the band setups \nwill be dependent one exactly where the complex develops, but \nthere will be the potential for it setting up over the area. \nThere also could be the potential for some strong storms late \nThursday night into Friday with damaging wind gusts the main \nrisk with any line segments that can develop. Shower and \nthunderstorms will linger into Friday night ending from west to \neast on Saturday as the trough moves off to the east. \n\nA cooler air mass will move into the area behind the trough on\nSaturday as highs in the 70s to the middle 80s are expected.\nTemperatures will warm back to near normal for this time of\nyear by early next week as highs in the upper 80s to the lower\n90s are expected. Widespread rain chances are currently low \nlate this weekend into early next week.",
